1
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,530
Sixteen!

2
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:43,600
The King of Rebellion.

3
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,650
Seventeen!

4
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:50,890
Eighteen!

5
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:55,380
Nineteen!

6
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:05,620
Twenty!

7
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:09,130
Crap, I lost!

8
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:12,500
Wow, but he's so small!

9
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,750
He's still holding on!

10
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:18,570
Way to go, shorty!

11
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:22,480
I lost a ton of money
because of you, Drott!

12
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:25,050
What the hell are you doing?

13
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:28,050
Break this shrimp's skull already!

14
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:32,340
Something's not right.

15
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,810
I feel hardly any
resistance when I hit him.

16
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,030
Damn it.

17
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:45,790
I see. That messenger certainly
is used to taking a beating.

18
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:50,250
He's twisting his neck and hips
just before Drott's fists hit him,

19
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:52,800
thereby dispersing the impact away
from the core of his body.

20
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:56,990
His movements are subtle, too,

21
00:02:57,710 --> 00:03:00,240
so no one's noticed that
he's avoiding direct hits.

22
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,520
But Drott is a strong man.

23
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:07,750
At this rate, he can't last long.

24
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:12,020
Twenty-three!

25
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:16,180
Twenty-four!

26
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:17,430
Thorfinn...

27
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:25,220
But violence should be a last resort.

28
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:33,070
I want to learn to find that first method.

29
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:41,730
Is this the "first method"
you were talking about?

30
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,990
Not hitting him back. Simply enduring.

31
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:54,980
Is that how you're going
to live from now on?

32
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,990
What's going on? Is there a fight?

33
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,710
Hey, you.

34
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,790
Thorfinn?

35
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:23,970
Hey, stop!

36
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,760
What's this about?

37
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:30,320
He's got nothing to do with the farm!

38
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:33,270
Crap.

39
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,820
All right! That was a solid hit!

40
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:58,300
Thirty-two!

41
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,920
That made a crazy sound.

42
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:03,250
Is he dead?

43
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:05,980
Thorfinn!

44
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,800
What are you two doing?

45
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,320
I thought you left the farm already.

46
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,980
How did this happen?

47
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:30,830
If he can endure 100 of his punches, he'll
be allowed to speak directly to the king.

48
00:05:31,410 --> 00:05:34,310
That's the promise they made.

49
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:37,440
That's ridiculous.

50
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:40,910
He's doing this for the farm?

51
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,460
Enough of this. No more.

52
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:53,940
The farm will surrender.
The decision's been made.

53
00:05:55,740 --> 00:06:01,570
You idiot. You're unbelievably softhearted.

54
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:06,720
If talking could've resolved this,
we'd have done that already.

55
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:14,460
Are you sure about that?

56
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:22,850
Did you really put in the effort

57
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:31,120
to resolve this through conversation?

58
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:38,160
Once they drew their swords,

59
00:06:39,450 --> 00:06:44,770
you merely answered with your
own blades without thinking.

60
00:06:45,990 --> 00:06:49,880
That's 32 hits. We're handing out winnings.

61
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,880
Is he getting back up?

62
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,240
Hey, wait a second.

63
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:08,190
Why are you just
standing there, middle-part?

64
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:13,590
Your fists hurt less than
being bitten by a bug!

65
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:18,850
Sixty-eight more. Get it over with.

66
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:21,380
I'm a busy man.

67
00:07:22,670 --> 00:07:25,860
People are waiting for me!

68
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,550
Don't! This battle is already—.

69
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:47,210
Einar, if he keeps this up, he'll die.

70
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:29,190
Ninety-eight...

71
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:37,140
Ninety-nine...

72
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:44,880
One hundred.

73
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:17,510
Thorfinn, son of Thors.

74
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:21,810
I'm sorry I doubted you.

75
00:09:23,390 --> 00:09:24,900
You...

76
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:29,590
You are a true warrior.

77
00:09:36,570 --> 00:09:37,870
Chief Thegn...

78
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:44,410
This man once guarded His Majesty as we do.

79
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:49,300
Please permit Thorfinn
an audience with the king.

80
00:09:58,190 --> 00:10:02,800
You're small, but you're
well-trained, Thorfinn.

81
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:07,010
Why didn't you strike back?

82
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:14,070
Beating Drott would have proven
that you are a former guard.

83
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:18,970
What kind of question is that?

84
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:23,710
I can't hit someone when
I'm trying to negotiate for peace.

85
00:10:24,860 --> 00:10:28,510
I just met all of you today.

86
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:32,500
We don't know anything about each other.

87
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,670
We have no reason to hate each other.

88
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:39,720
So why do we have to
hit each other? It's stupid.

89
00:10:40,830 --> 00:10:44,290
It's just Canute and Ketil
who are feuding with each other.

90
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:49,860
The two leaders could settle this
over a game of hnefatafl.

91
00:10:50,310 --> 00:10:55,400
There's no need to gather all these men
and shed all this blood.

92
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,440
We just met today.

93
00:11:05,310 --> 00:11:07,730
You are not my enemies.

94
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:24,790
I don't have any enemies.

95
00:11:34,290 --> 00:11:42,900
You're a bold man to reject war while
surrounded by this many professional soldiers.

96
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,460
But...

97
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:50,050
Ketil and His Majesty
should play hnefatafl, huh?

98
00:11:51,090 --> 00:11:53,010
What's so funny?

99
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:58,960
Sorry. You should try suggesting
that to His Majesty yourself.

100
00:12:00,210 --> 00:12:04,640
He doesn't go to war because he wants to.

101
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:09,970
Once you see him and hear what he has
to say, you'll realize what's in his heart.

102
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:16,020
Clear the way.

103
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:19,070
I'm permitting this messenger
an audience with His Majesty.

104
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:31,040
Come on, Einar.

105
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:36,420
We're going to see the man who starts wars.

106
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:39,830
Don't you have things
you want to say to him, too?

107
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,430
Y-Yeah.

108
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:46,770
You bet I do. A whole mountain of them.

109
00:13:24,850 --> 00:13:29,350
Are all of them casualties of this battle?

110
00:13:30,770 --> 00:13:32,830
Don't look, Einar.

111
00:13:34,650 --> 00:13:35,940
Pater...

112
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:38,180
Don't look.

113
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:44,070
If you find Pater among the dead,
you won't be able to remain calm.

114
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:19,540
Very well. I'll see him.

115
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:22,870
I'll respect the feelings of
yourself and the men.

116
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:24,290
Thank you.

117
00:14:26,010 --> 00:14:28,160
Messenger, approach.

118
00:14:58,430 --> 00:14:59,940
So you're still alive.

119
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:04,610
It's been a while, Thorfinn.

120
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:11,680
You must hate me for making you a slave...

121
00:15:13,690 --> 00:15:20,210
No... for what happened to Askeladd.

122
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:31,170
I'm still alive after drawing
a blade against Danish royalty.

123
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:35,780
I appreciate the
consideration you showed me.

124
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:41,650
I'm sorry about the scar on your face.

125
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:45,640
He's the man who
scarred His Majesty's face?

126
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:48,580
Thorfinn Karlsefni...

127
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:53,530
The man said to have been
an even match for Thorkell in combat.

128
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,750
I had no idea he was so small and young.

129
00:15:58,310 --> 00:16:00,910
You drew a blade against the king?

130
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:06,910
It's impossible to tell
who you are with that face,

131
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:10,100
but you seem to be the Thorfinn I know.

132
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:15,150
You've come to say some commendable things.

133
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:20,160
Four years, huh?

134
00:16:22,250 --> 00:16:25,950
It's already been four years since then.

135
00:16:27,410 --> 00:16:31,630
That's enough time for a person to change.

136
00:16:39,770 --> 00:16:43,150
Canute, I'd like you to leave the farm.

137
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:45,250
I can't do that.

138
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:49,330
Ketil's clan started this dispute.

139
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:57,540
Ketil's son Olmar killed ten of my men
because I wouldn't make him one of my thegns.

140
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,290
I've heard about that.

141
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,630
But you've made your point.

142
00:17:03,110 --> 00:17:06,060
More than 100 of the farm's men have died.

143
00:17:06,570 --> 00:17:12,070
This region may not be able to recover
now that so many of its workers are dead.

144
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:16,960
I advised them to surrender.

145
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:21,200
It's Ketil's fault for miscalculating the
difference in the strength of our forces.

146
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:26,790
This battle cannot end until
Ketil's clan has been dealt with.

147
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:33,270
In other words, it won't end
until you've captured this farm.

148
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:37,380
Make all the excuses you want.
You can't hide it.

149
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:41,570
You call yourself a king,
but you're actually just a thief.

150
00:17:42,430 --> 00:17:47,550
How are you any different
from the average Viking chief?

151
00:17:49,050 --> 00:17:53,190
If you want a farm that badly,
then start one yourself.

152
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:58,560
Till the land, watch over it,
and raise your own crops.

153
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,540
Then you'll understand firsthand

154
00:18:02,270 --> 00:18:08,290
what a terrible thing it is to
take that from someone else.

155
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:13,310
Canute.

156
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:18,180
You once told me at Gainsborough...

157
00:18:19,790 --> 00:18:22,080
that you'd build a paradise in this place.

158
00:18:22,910 --> 00:18:26,240
A utopia for those who suffer.

159
00:18:29,070 --> 00:18:32,210
Do you still believe that?

160
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:37,010
A chief, huh?

161
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:43,140
Indeed. I am the chief of Viking chiefs.

162
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:48,110
I am the sovereign king...

163
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:51,410
The most powerful Viking on the North Sea.

164
00:18:53,290 --> 00:18:56,500
The ruler of the largest territory
in Northern Europe.

165
00:18:57,290 --> 00:19:01,310
The commander who leads a
thousand ships and ten thousand men.

166
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:06,600
My power exceeds human understanding
and makes the impossible possible.

167
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:11,470
Behold.

168
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:15,740
With my power, I shall stop those waves.

169
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:24,870
In the name of King Canute,
waves, I command you to stop.

170
00:19:42,990 --> 00:19:47,250
Did you bear witness to my strength?

171
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:51,860
I am powerless to stop
even the approaching waves.

172
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:57,780
Do you know who drives those waves?

173
00:20:05,610 --> 00:20:06,690
God does.

174
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:15,330
Building a paradise on Earth
means defying His logic.

175
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:18,480
It's an act of rebellion against God.

176
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:25,270
Humankind cannot find
happiness under God's rule.

177
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:29,060
Rebellion...

178
00:20:29,850 --> 00:20:31,990
Look at us, Thorfinn.

179
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:35,360
Look at us Vikings.

180
00:20:36,270 --> 00:20:39,060
We're responsible for this
chaos and destruction.

181
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:41,350
We're fearsome raiders.

182
00:20:42,650 --> 00:20:46,670
Do you think we deserve
to live in paradise?

183
00:20:47,870 --> 00:20:51,370
But that is what humans are.

184
00:20:52,030 --> 00:20:57,390
Committing sins as we wander lost
is precisely what humans do.

185
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:05,700
Unless I save these people abandoned by
God, I'll never be able to build a paradise.

186
00:21:08,490 --> 00:21:11,520
Save the Vikings?

187
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:13,390
Yes.

188
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:23,030
I am the only one capable of conquering
them, ruling them, unifying their strength,

189
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:25,530
and directing them towards paradise.

190
00:21:26,250 --> 00:21:28,100
I need strength.

191
00:21:29,410 --> 00:21:35,840
I will unify the strength
of all humankind to fight God.

192
00:21:42,930 --> 00:21:45,930
Canute is an incredible man.

193
00:21:46,850 --> 00:21:51,680
It never even occurred to me
to save the Vikings.

194
00:21:53,730 --> 00:21:56,310
I'm gonna knock this guy on his ass.

195
00:21:56,830 --> 00:22:00,820
You're free to pursue
whatever huge goals you want.

196
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:06,660
But who's gonna save all the people
you kill today for your goals?

197
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:10,260
Will you let the Vikings live
because they can help you,

198
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:14,020
while killing and stealing from people
who aren't useful to you?

199
00:22:14,770 --> 00:22:17,680
Building a paradise, my ass!

200
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:26,720
King Ethelred burned down my village,
and King Sweyn killed my family.

201
00:22:27,730 --> 00:22:31,430
I don't care what their ideals were.

202
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:35,140
I've had enough.

203
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:39,840
I refuse to suffer any more because of you.

204
00:22:46,810 --> 00:22:48,320
Hate me if you must.

205
00:22:49,020 --> 00:22:51,300
I won't seek your forgiveness.

206
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:55,440
What did you say?

207
00:22:56,670 --> 00:22:58,070
Don't, Einar.

208
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:05,710
Canute, I'll ask you again.

209
00:23:06,430 --> 00:23:09,010
You really have no intention
of leaving this farm?

210
00:23:09,370 --> 00:23:13,760
No. I need Ketil's wealth
for my undertaking.

211
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:18,690
What will you do, Thorfinn?

212
00:23:19,490 --> 00:23:22,630
Will you kill me here?

213
00:23:25,830 --> 00:23:30,280
For you cannot stop me unless you kill me.

214
00:25:35,990 --> 00:25:40,120
Two Paths.

215
00:25:37,370 --> 00:25:38,990
"Two Paths."
